problems.problem:
Let $m\ge 2$ and $n$ be positive integers. The set $S(m,n)$ consists of all polynomials $P(x)$ whose coefficients belong to the set $\{0,1,2,\dots,m^2-1\}$ and which satisfy the condition $P(m)=n$. Find the number of elements of the set $S(m,n)$ when
(a) $n=10m$;
(b) $n=m^2$;
(c) $n$ is an arbitrary positive integer.

An infinite sequence of positive integers $a_1,a_2,a_3,\dots$ satisfies the following conditions:
(i) $2<a_1<a_2<a_3<\dots$;
(ii) for every term $a_i$ of the sequence, all its divisors greater than $2$ are also terms of this sequence;
(iii) for every pair of terms $(a_i,a_j)$, $i\neq j$, the number $a_ia_j+1$ is also a term of this sequence.
Determine all such sequences.
